sentence:
I hold it true, whate’er befall;
⁠I feel it, when I sorrow most;
⁠’Tis better to have loved and lost
Than never to have loved at all.

Ye wolde wepe at every mele;
But for my sone wepe ye never a dele.
You would weep at every meal, but for my son you never weep a deal.

A fals double tunge is more fiers and fell
Then Cerberus the cur couching in the kenel of hel;
Wherof hereafter, I thinke for to write,

How gay the Habitations that adorn
This fertile Valley! Not a House but seems
To give assurance of content within;

HERO. Good Margaret, run thee to the parlour;
There shalt thou find my cousin Beatrice
Proposing with the prince and Claudio

[…] the quick comedians
Extemporally will stage us, and present
Our Alexandrian revels;

“My husband, alas! whom I now (sob, sob) mourn,
A short time since (sob) to this grave (sob) was borne;
And (sob) he lies buried in this (sob, sob) grave.”
